{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1115346-can-a-mage-cast-a-spell-while-being-possessed-by-a-spirit","id":1115346,"title":"Can a mage cast a spell while being possessed by a Spirit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-12T20:15:52-07:00","id":1115346,"title":"Can a mage cast a spell while being possessed by a Spirit?","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I was wondering. I have a mage that got possessed by a spirit, for the sake a roleplay I let the mage be conscious and talk to the spirit. <br /> <br /> Now the Mage is asking if he is able to cast a spell while possessed, more specifically exorcism or something similar.<br /> <br /> I am inclined to say yes... but perhaps with major penalties. What do you think? It worries me this might set a precedent that Possession is easy to circumvent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo","name":"rluengo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:27:53-07:00","id":1115349,"title":"","content":"With Possession, 'Living hosts are put into a coma-like state while being possessed.' Mages can't cast spells in comas.<br /> <br /> Obviously you're free to do what you want, but allowing mages to cast spells like exorcism while possessed is going to severely weaken what possession does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:50:17-07:00","id":1115361,"title":"","content":"Aaaaactually, even in a coma, the situation is not quite as certain as all that. If the mage's soul can engage, it can still cast a spell. You are generally in some deep weirdness and storyteller territory, of course, but for mages who surf alternate states of consciousness regularly, it starts to become more likely that they <i>are </i>able to function than <i>not</i>.<br /> (In 1e, I seem to recall a merit that allowed meditation when penalized or not normally possible. That would permit casting a spell from within Astral Space.)<br /> <br /> While trapped inside one's soul, you could allow <i>Exorcism</i> to boot it, but only once you find its representation in the Oneiros, first. Takes it from a 'get out of possession cheap' card to 'pad my story with a quest, muahahaha' if you allow the possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:51:55-07:00","id":1115362,"title":"","content":"Probably not if you mostly want to stick with default possession rules, but there're some fun directions you could take it with a little house-ruling. Something like letting the mage cast relatively freely <i>if</i> the spell actively aligns with the spirit's desires and/or Influence (whether or not you let the spirit attempt a weird form of teamwork roll or provide some other bonus is your call, of course), but calling for a Clash of Wills or something similar if they're trying to work against it like you're describing. All depends on how... &quot;interesting&quot; you want to make things for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 07-12-2017, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:03:51-07:00","id":1115366,"title":"","content":"Since you've already houseruled possession we'd have to do an evaluation of the situation. Since spells come into being from imagos, and imagos are formed mentally, a mage that is conscious should always be able to cast a spell (unless something is specifically messing around with the mage's ability to cast spells). However, the only Yantra the mage could reasonably employ are those that doesn't require physical control of your body. Only places, concentration (though the spirit might be able to interrupt the concentration by a contested roll of some kind) and Persona could be used as Yantras. Additionally, I happen to recall that casting a spell in a grapple will levy a -3 dice penalty to the spellcasting roll if the mage loses the grappling roll due to being overpowered by the opponent. Since the mage is quite clearly overpowered by the spirit that penalty could apply in this situation.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming the mage is a PC so I get not wanting to remove all agency from a player, however the mind is the most powerful weapon a mage has so it was a bit brash. But you could solve that problem by allowing the spirit to control whether or not the victim is conscious. If the spirit realises the mage is starting to cast a spell and can reflexively put the mage in a coma-like state as a response then you functionally allow the player some agency while removing the huge problem it'd otherwise cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T02:38:46-07:00","id":1115438,"title":"","content":"I'd think the answer is <i>usually</i> no, but with a certain caveat. A mage <i>typically</i> needs to be able to think to cast magic, so in general, a mage who is possessed cannot think and therefore can't cast. <i>But</i>, IIRC in a previous discussions about cutting mages off from thinking/using their magic, it was stated that while it might work for a while, because magic is just as much an expression of the soul you'd more likely than not turn them into something like one of the Mad. Without the ability to consciously control their magic, their magic would instead eventually become completely unshackled and act purely in accordance with their Obsessions.<br /> <br /> I would assume that eventually, without a guiding consciousness to control their use of magic, they would begin using magic without restraint in order to fulfill the mages Obsessions, without regard for what the spirit possessing them would want and beyond that spirits ability to control. It would almost certainly end horribly for everyone involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-13-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T04:27:36-07:00","id":1115463,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, but in this particular example Possession was houseruled to allow the mage to be conscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:40:33-07:00","id":1115504,"title":"","content":"I think that even if Spirit possesion works exactly as described within the books, there can be lots of Spirit-like entities that play along different rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T07:55:56-07:00","id":1115528,"title":"","content":"If a mage can think, the mage can cast spells. That said?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Casting During a Grapple</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can cast spells in a single turn without making any outward sign. A mage in a grapple (whether he initiated it or not) can cast a spell whether he wins the grapple check for the turn or not, but suffers a \u20133 penalty to the spellcasting roll if he lost. Mages in a grapple cannot employ any Yantras involving movement, but if the grapple was initiated part-way through casting a spell, any Yantras the caster has already spent turns incorporating into the spell have their full effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given we're talking about possession, and not just grappling, I'd inflict a full -5 penalty. Couple that with the spirit's Withstand and the almost definite lack of Yantra (I'd allow a rote and concentration, but no mantra, mudra, place or tools. Or ritual bonus from long time casting). See if the spell can go through. If yes, the mage &quot;fights off the possession.&quot; If not? The magus is still trapped. Then, if the mage fails, have the spirit &quot;punish&quot; the mage in some way for fighting back and see if that discourges them. Maybe do the drop-unconcious thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T07:55:56-07:00","id":1115529,"title":"","content":"these double posts are getting annoying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T08:31:50-07:00","id":1115540,"title":"","content":"I don't think the mage can cast spells in the Material world while unconscious... Whether they can spells while within their own Oneiros* while possessed would be a judgement call if that type of unconsciousness allows dreams. If so, then interesting weirdness, if not then frightening helplessness.<br /> <br /> As a ST I'd make the call based on the themes of the game;<br /> <br /> A Protagonist Empowerment Fantasy style would justify choosing that the possessed do indeed dream and thus doesn't rob all power, just adding a layer to the hero's journey which includes delving within.<br /> <br /> Darker Lovecraftian cosmic horror and existential dread would totally make choosing helplessness the best choice.<br /> <br /> Both are valid but once the judgement call is made it should remain consistent, they don't mix well unless you want players to feel betrayed about the loss of their Empowerment Fantasy they bought into.<br /> <br /> *=And thus have a chance to either face the possessing entity within the Oneiros, or escape their dream via Astral travel and magic shenanigans to otherwise get at their possessor, perhaps possessing another, find a way to manifest in the material from the Astral, or other out of the box solutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-13-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:49:39-07:00","id":1115591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1115346-can-a-mage-cast-a-spell-while-being-possessed-by-a-spirit?p=1115528#post1115528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage can think, the mage can cast spells. That said?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Given we're talking about possession, and not just grappling, I'd inflict a full -5 penalty. Couple that with the spirit's Withstand and the almost definite lack of Yantra (I'd allow <b>a rote</b> and concentration, but no mantra, <b>mudra</b>, place or tools. Or ritual bonus from long time casting). See if the spell can go through. If yes, the mage &quot;fights off the possession.&quot; If not? The magus is still trapped. Then, if the mage fails, have the spirit &quot;punish&quot; the mage in some way for fighting back and see if that discourges them. Maybe do the drop-unconcious thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you're actually confused or if the post is just unclear, but for the record: the +Skill bonus from a Rote comes from the use of a Mudra. You can use Rotes without Mudras for the free Reach, lack of Mana cost and in special circumstances rote quality on the roll, but if you can't control your body you don't get the bonus dice.<br /> Also I think I'd allow Place Yantra. I see no fluff or crunch reason a mage couldn't benefit from a Verge or simple ambient symbolism without bodily control, and luring the possessing spirit into an appropriate location to help the mage break free makes for an interesting story.<br /> <br /> As for the situation at hand, I pretty much agree with everything that's been said. I particularly like the idea of playing out some kind of struggle in the Oneiros, especially if the mage in question is an avid oneironaut and/or versed in Mind or Spirit. If you're up for it you could even represent outside aid as changes in the internal world, e.g. friends doing the &quot;I know you're in there!&quot; routine manifest as cheering crowds giving a morale boost or someone casting a Mind Shielding spell manifests as shining armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:55:55-07:00","id":1115617,"title":"","content":"Is the mage permitting the use of his body, or is the spirit possessing him without the will of the mage? The reason I ask, is because if the mage is the willing participant, he can utilize shielding spells to keep his mind conscious when his body is possessed by another's will - among other things. Utilizing such a spell, I would grant no penalties to spellcasting from things like grappling and other things. Now - I totally understand they are -already- possessed, but I figured I'd mention it just in case for your player (as if it's a case of 'I didn't take precautions' there is a lesson to be learned! :P)<br /> <br /> If, however, the mage is not a willing individual then I would probably not allow the casting. There is nothing in particular stopping a mage from casting in the Onieros - except, that if I'm not mistaken such an endeavor would require external factors (a hallow, demesne, iris) to allow the mage to be there. Since a mage is not supposed to be conscious to begin with, and they were not in such an environment - the mage may need to rely on his allies to bail him out... or, since this is slightly houseruled, convince the spirit to go to a suitable location where they can reach their onieros - which could be good for story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T14:30:50-07:00","id":1115677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1115346-can-a-mage-cast-a-spell-while-being-possessed-by-a-spirit?p=1115463#post1115463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting, but in this particular example Possession was houseruled to allow the mage to be conscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they are conscious enough to think they're probably conscious enough to be able to use their magic. If they aren't conscious enough to think they'll probably eventually lose conscious control of their magic. Regardless, except for short term possession that ends in the death of the possessed mage (and almost certainly even then) the spirit is going to come to regret its life choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T01:20:57-07:00","id":1116292,"title":"","content":"From my understanding, it depends on the mage's consiousness, subconsious (oneiros) and the spell's range of effect. All the cases assume that the mage was unprepared of the possession<br /> a) The possessed mage looses consiousness but the possessing entity has extra powers to block even his subconsious. Such a mage has effectively no oneiros (or a &quot;frozen&quot; oneiros) and is completelly helpless for the duration of the possession (usually a scene and remember it costs the entity 3 Essence each time), unable to cast any spells of his own. This is a rare/powerful kind of possession fiting for the aforementioned Lovercraftian horrors and other God-like entities (the Kings Above).<br /> b) The possessed mage looses consiousness but he has access to his subconsious and thus his oneiros (under my understanting all mages have access to their Oneira and only need places of power to start Astral Paths beyond them. Alternatively, assume the entity happened to stay for some time in a place alowing Astral Travel). Upon entering his oneiros the mage can either target himself or (as mentioned above) search the repressentation of the possessing force in his mind and target that instead. Both with the right combination of spells (target self to teleport near creature's bane, mark own flesh with letters asking for help, trap the entity into an oneiric prison, oreiricly blast it out, etc) can help with the situation directly or otherwise.<br /> Note: I don't remember where I read it, but it was mentioned that while inside your Oneiros you can cast spells on your physical self and anything inside your mind (and anything inside your mind has a representation in your oneiros)<br /> c) The possessed mage somehow manages to remain consious. Though rare, people with Legacies or experienced Mind casters can manage it. In such a weird case, not only can they cast in the physical world regardless of the entity's possession but are possibly entitled to a clash of wills for each action against their will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 07-15-2017, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:37:45-07:00","id":1116379,"title":"","content":"I have to point out that in B, if the mage isn't conscious they can't enter their Oneiros since doing so is a conscious action. If the mage didn't enter the Astral before the possession happened they'd be just as helpless as in A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:14:20-07:00","id":1116456,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6169\" data-vbnamecard=\"6169\">Shadowjim12</a> You have to form an Astral Path to your Oneiros, so you'd have to be in a place of power to access it. You need a place of power to access any level of the Astral deeper than the dreams of people who are asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:43:23-07:00","id":1117728,"title":"","content":"This happened in a game of mine. The cabal got inside a bus that was taking the souls of suicidal passengers and building its influence as king of the road spirits in the city. They took a few precautions and intended to negotiate, but things got heated and plans derailed (they decided they didn't want to keep a promise with the bus because it would require them to sacrifice some Wisdom and they were already low). Long story short, they ended causing a major traffic accident and when the Acanthus tried to undo that, the spirit possessed him to stop him. He couldn't cast any spells, but just taking him out of the picture for one combat was a dire circumstance. They eventually beat the spirit out of him and bound it in the Shadow under their Demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T14:07:45-07:00","id":1120068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1115346-can-a-mage-cast-a-spell-while-being-possessed-by-a-spirit?p=1115617#post1115617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the mage permitting the use of his body, or is the spirit possessing him without the will of the mage? The reason I ask, is because if the mage is the willing participant, he can utilize shielding spells to keep his mind conscious when his body is possessed by another's will - among other things. Utilizing such a spell, I would grant no penalties to spellcasting from things like grappling and other things. Now - I totally understand they are -already- possessed, but I figured I'd mention it just in case for your player (as if it's a case of 'I didn't take precautions' there is a lesson to be learned! :P)<br /> <br /> If, however, the mage is not a willing individual then I would probably not allow the casting. There is nothing in particular stopping a mage from casting in the Onieros - except, that if I'm not mistaken such an endeavor would require external factors (a hallow, demesne, iris) to allow the mage to be there. Since a mage is not supposed to be conscious to begin with, and they were not in such an environment - the mage may need to rely on his allies to bail him out... or, since this is slightly houseruled, convince the spirit to go to a suitable location where they can reach their onieros - which could be good for story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Going into your onieros requires conscious effort. If the mage was in his onieros or astral projecting beforehand he can do this if not he's screwed. Considering he's a thyrsus, he really has no one to blame but himself. The rules don't allow it and shouldn't really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}